{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Aaron shall burn upon it.</b> One must say that 'Aaron' is not literal, since the incense offering is valid even with an ordinary priest, as we say in the chapter אמר להם הממונה: 'New ones for the incense — come and draw lots.' And furthermore, from the fact that it is written ״ובהעלות אהרן״ etc. — ״he shall burn it״ — since it ties the incense to the lamps, anyone qualified for the kindling of the lamps is qualified for the incense, and regarding the lamps it is written ״יערוך אותו אהרן ובניו״. And furthermore, one may say that from ״ובהעלות״ it is not literal, for it is written ״יערוך אותו אהרן ובניו״ in another place; likewise here too, ״and Aaron shall burn upon it״ is not literal."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:19.306379913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}